| [[File:Logo En Marche !.svg|140px|Logo of En Marche!]]
| The youngest candidate in the race and a former cabinet member who had never run for elected office, Macron described himself as "neither of the right nor the left". He was appointed deputy Secretary-General of the [[Élysée Palace|Élysée]] in 2012 and became [[Ministry of the Economy and Finance (France)|Economy Minister]] in 2014, lending his name to the "Macron law" to promote economic growth and opportunities. He founded the [[La République En Marche!|En Marche!]] movement in April 2016 before resigning from the cabinet on 30 August.<ref name="candidates"/> The most explicitly pro-European of the candidates, Macron intends to implement reforms to modernize the French economy.<ref name="candidates-figaro"/> Macron secured support across the political spectrum, but primarily among liberal-leaning figures;<ref>{{cite news|author1=Anne-Aël Durand|author2=Pierre Breteau|title=Gauche, centre, droite, milieux économiques ou société civile : qui sont les soutiens d'Emmanuel Macron ?|url=http://www.lemonde.fr/les-decodeurs/article/2017/03/09/gauche-centre-droite-milieux-economiques-ou-societe-civile-qui-sont-les-soutiens-d-emmanuel-macron_5092220_4355770.html|newspaper=Le Monde|date=9 March 2017|access-date=3 April 2017|archive-date=2 April 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170402101253/http://www.lemonde.fr/les-decodeurs/article/2017/03/09/gauche-centre-droite-milieux-economiques-ou-societe-civile-qui-sont-les-soutiens-d-emmanuel-macron_5092220_4355770.html|url-status=live}}</ref> notable supporters include perennial centrist candidate [[François Bayrou]], president of the [[Democratic Movement (France)|Democratic Movement]] (MoDem),<ref name="Bayrou"/> as well as [[Minister of the Armed Forces (France)|Minister of Defence]] [[Jean-Yves Le Drian]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Exclusif. Le Drian annonce son soutien à Macron ce jeudi|url=http://www.ouest-france.fr/elections/presidentielle/exclusif-jean-yves-le-drian-annonce-son-soutien-emmanuel-macron-4878523|newspaper=Ouest-France|date=23 March 2017|access-date=3 April 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170329114947/http://www.ouest-france.fr/elections/presidentielle/exclusif-jean-yves-le-drian-annonce-son-soutien-emmanuel-macron-4878523|archive-date=29 March 2017}}</ref>
