[[File:French Election- Celebrations at The Louvre, Paris (33707026433).jpg|thumb|right|250px|Supporters of Macron celebrating his victory at the [[Louvre]] on 7 May]]
After being eliminated in the first round, both [[François Fillon]] and [[Benoît Hamon]] called to vote for [[Emmanuel Macron]], while [[Jean-Luc Mélenchon]] refused to pronounce in favor of either candidate, preferring to first consult activists from his movement.<ref name="live-20170423">{{cite news|title=Présidentielle 2017 : revivez la soirée électorale du premier tour|url=http://www.lemonde.fr/election-presidentielle-2017/live/2017/04/23/presidentielle-2017-resultats-analyses-reactions-suivez-la-soiree-du-premier-tour-en-direct_5115904_4854003.html|newspaper=Le Monde|date=23 April 2017|access-date=28 April 2017|archive-date=11 October 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171011051803/http://www.lemonde.fr//election-presidentielle-2017/live/2017/04/23/presidentielle-2017-resultats-analyses-reactions-suivez-la-soiree-du-premier-tour-en-direct_5115904_4854003.html|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Jean Lassalle]] and [[Nathalie Arthaud]] opted to cast a [[protest vote|blank vote]],<ref name="live-20170423"/><ref name="Lassalle-blanc">{{cite news|title=DIRECT. Présidentielle : Jean Lassalle votera blanc au second tour|url=http://www.ouest-france.fr/elections/presidentielle/direct-presidentielle-le-pen-renforcee-par-l-episode-whirlpool-4955884|newspaper=Ouest-France|date=28 April 2017|access-date=28 April 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170428094112/http://www.ouest-france.fr/elections/presidentielle/direct-presidentielle-le-pen-renforcee-par-l-episode-whirlpool-4955884|archive-date=28 April 2017}}</ref> [[Philippe Poutou]] and [[François Asselineau]] gave no voting instructions,<ref name="live-20170423"/> and [[Jacques Cheminade]] only stated that he would personally refuse to vote for Le Pen and denounced the forces of "financial occupation".<ref name="Cheminade"/> [[Nicolas Dupont-Aignan]] endorsed Le Pen during the evening of 28 April,<ref name="NDA-MLP"/> and was subsequently revealed as her choice for Prime Minister the following day.<ref>{{cite news|title=Marine Le Pen annonce qu'elle nommera Nicolas Dupont-Aignan Premier ministre si elle est élue|url=http://www.bfmtv.com/politique/marine-le-pen-annonce-qu-elle-nommera-nicolas-dupont-aignan-premier-ministre-si-elle-est-elue-1153450.html|publisher=BFM TV|date=29 April 2017|access-date=30 April 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170429125747/http://www.bfmtv.com/politique/marine-le-pen-annonce-qu-elle-nommera-nicolas-dupont-aignan-premier-ministre-si-elle-est-elue-1153450.html|archive-date=29 April 2017}}</ref> On 2 May, the result of Mélenchon's consultation was published, with 36.12% voting for a blank vote, 34.83% supporting a vote for Macron, and 29.05% opting to abstain;<ref>{{cite news|author=Charlie Vandekerkhove|title=Les militants de la France insoumise plébiscitent le vote blanc ou l'abstention au second tour|url=http://www.bfmtv.com/politique/la-france-insoumise-devoile-le-resultat-de-sa-consultation-sur-le-second-tour-1155324.html|agency=Agence France-Presse|publisher=BFM TV|date=2 May 2017|access-date=2 May 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170502192106/http://www.bfmtv.com/politique/la-france-insoumise-devoile-le-resultat-de-sa-consultation-sur-le-second-tour-1155324.html|archive-date= 2 May 2017}}</ref> Mélenchon, for his part, issued no voting instructions, only urging his supporters not to make the "terrible error" of voting for Le Pen.<ref>{{cite news|title=Présidentielle : deux tiers des Insoumis de Mélenchon choisissent le vote blanc ou l'abstention|url=http://www.leparisien.fr/elections/presidentielle/presidentielle-les-insoumis-de-melenchon-choisissent-de-voter-blanc-a-36-02-05-2017-6909717.php|newspaper=Le Parisien|date=2 May 2017|access-date=7 May 2017|archive-date=2 May 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170502184623/http://www.leparisien.fr/elections/presidentielle/presidentielle-les-insoumis-de-melenchon-choisissent-de-voter-blanc-a-36-02-05-2017-6909717.php|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Jean-Marie Le Pen]] supported his daughter.<ref>{{cite news|author=Arthur Berdah|title="Moi, je vote Marine", annonce Jean-Marie Le Pen|url=http://www.lefigaro.fr/elections/presidentielles/2017/04/17/35003-20170417ARTFIG00049-moi-je-vote-marine-annonce-jean-marie-le-pen.php|newspaper=Le Figaro|date=17 April 2017|access-date=1 May 2017|archive-date=7 May 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170507233454/http://www.lefigaro.fr/elections/presidentielles/2017/04/17/35003-20170417ARTFIG00049-moi-je-vote-marine-annonce-jean-marie-le-pen.php|url-status=live}}</ref>

[[File:Macron and Le Pen Voting Cards.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Voting cards for the second round.]]
On the evening of the first round, Macron and members of his entourage celebrated the result at ''[[Café de la Rotonde|La Rotonde]]'', a ''[[brasserie]]'' in the [[6th arrondissement of Paris]]; the move was criticized as premature and complacent, viewed as reminiscent of [[Nicolas Sarkozy]]'s widely criticized post-election celebration at ''[[Fouquet's]]'' in 2007.<ref>{{cite news|title=Le " moment de cœur " de Macron à La Rotonde se mêle aux souvenirs du Fouquet's de Sarkozy|url=http://www.lemonde.fr/big-browser/article/2017/04/24/le-moment-de-c-ur-de-macron-a-la-rotonde-se-mele-aux-souvenirs-du-fouquet-s-de-sarkozy_5116597_4832693.html|newspaper=Le Monde|date=24 April 2017|access-date=27 April 2017|archive-date=25 April 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170425114213/http://www.lemonde.fr/big-browser/article/2017/04/24/le-moment-de-c-ur-de-macron-a-la-rotonde-se-mele-aux-souvenirs-du-fouquet-s-de-sarkozy_5116597_4832693.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On 24 April, Le Pen vacated her position as leader of the National Front on 24 April to focus on her presidential candidacy but remained a member of the party.<ref>{{cite news|title=Marine Le Pen se " met en congé de la présidence du Front national "|url=http://www.lemonde.fr/election-presidentielle-2017/article/2017/04/24/marine-le-pen-se-met-en-conge-de-la-presidence-du-front-national_5116791_4854003.html|newspaper=Le Monde|date=24 April 2017|access-date=26 April 2017|archive-date=9 April 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230409042302/https://www.lemonde.fr/election-presidentielle-2017/article/2017/04/24/marine-le-pen-se-met-en-conge-de-la-presidence-du-front-national_5116791_4854003.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On 26 April, while Macron met with union representatives in his hometown of [[Amiens]] employed at the local [[Whirlpool Corporation|Whirlpool]] factory, slated to close in 2018, Le Pen arrived at the site of the factory outdoors around noon in a visit to speak with workers, catching Macron by surprise. When Macron subsequently arrived at the factory site in mid-afternoon, he was whistled and heckled by a hostile crowd, with some shouting "Marine présidente", before he subsequently spoke with the workers for half an hour.<ref>{{cite news|title=Whirlpool : la folle journée d'Emmanuel Macron et Marine Le Pen en quatre actes|url=http://www.francetvinfo.fr/politique/emmanuel-macron/whirlpool-le-bras-de-fer-entre-emmanuel-macron-et-marine-le-pen-en-quatre-actes_2162846.html|publisher=franceinfo|date=26 April 2017|access-date=27 April 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170427012157/http://www.francetvinfo.fr/politique/emmanuel-macron/whirlpool-le-bras-de-fer-entre-emmanuel-macron-et-marine-le-pen-en-quatre-actes_2162846.html|archive-date=27 April 2017}}</ref>

The official campaign ended at midnight on 5 May.<ref>{{cite news|title=Revivez le dernier jour de la campagne présidentielle|url=http://www.lemonde.fr/election-presidentielle-2017/live/2017/05/05/presidentielle-en-direct-dernier-jour-de-campagne-pour-emmanuel-macron-et-marine-le-pen_5122576_4854003.html|newspaper=Le Monde|date=5 May 2017|access-date=5 May 2017|archive-date=5 May 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170505070244/http://www.lemonde.fr//election-presidentielle-2017/live/2017/05/05/presidentielle-en-direct-dernier-jour-de-campagne-pour-emmanuel-macron-et-marine-le-pen_5122576_4854003.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Just minutes before the election silence went into effect, [[2017 Macron e-mail leaks|emails and documents from the Macron campaign were leaked]] on a file-sharing website. The campaign team subsequently issued a statement claiming that they had been compromised, and alleged that the leak contained both real as well and some fabricated documents. Numerama, an online publication focusing on digital life, described the leaked material as "utterly mundane", consisting of "the contents of a hard drive and several emails of co-workers and En Marche political officials." Leaked documents included "memos, bills, loans for amounts that are hardly over-the-top, recommendations and other reservations, amidst, of course, exchanges that are strictly personal and private — personal notes on the rain and sunshine, a confirmation email for the publishing of a book, reservation of a table for friends, etc.", in addition to some documents unrelated to Macron.<ref>{{cite news|author=Julien Cadot|title=#MacronLeaks : à 24h du vote, des opposants au candidat En Marche jouent leurs dernières cartes|url=http://www.numerama.com/politique/255850-macronleaks-a-24h-du-vote-des-opposants-au-candidat-en-marche-jouent-leurs-dernieres-cartes.html|publisher=Numerama|date=5 May 2017|access-date=7 May 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170506180719/http://www.numerama.com/politique/255850-macronleaks-a-24h-du-vote-des-opposants-au-candidat-en-marche-jouent-leurs-dernieres-cartes.html|archive-date= 6 May 2017}}</ref><!-- translation sourced from https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/world/europe/france-macron-hacking.html -->

Voting in the second round took place on Saturday 6 May from 08:00 to 19:00 (local time) in the [[Overseas France|French overseas departments and territories]] situated east of the [[International Date Line]] and west of [[metropolitan France]] (i.e. [[French Guiana]], [[French Polynesia]], [[Guadeloupe]], [[Martinique]], [[Collectivity of Saint Martin|Saint Martin]], [[Saint Barthélemy]] and [[Saint Pierre and Miquelon]]), as well as at [[List of diplomatic missions of France|French diplomatic missions]] in the [[Americas]]. Voting in [[metropolitan France]] (as well as the French overseas departments and territories of [[Mayotte]], [[New Caledonia]], [[Réunion]] and [[Wallis and Futuna]], and [[List of diplomatic missions of France|French diplomatic missions]] outside the [[Americas]]) took place on Sunday 7 May from 08:00 to 19:00 or 20:00 (local time).<ref name="CircularINTA1702262C"/> The results of the second round were officially proclaimed on 10 May.<ref>{{cite web|title=Communiqué sur l'annonce des résultats officiels du second tour de l'élection présidentielle|url=http://www.conseil-constitutionnel.fr/conseil-constitutionnel/francais/actualites/2017/communique-sur-l-annonce-des-resultats-officiels-du-second-tour-de-l-election-presidentielle.148975.html|publisher=Conseil constitutionnel|date=5 May 2017|access-date=8 May 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170508154225/http://www.conseil-constitutionnel.fr/conseil-constitutionnel/francais/actualites/2017/communique-sur-l-annonce-des-resultats-officiels-du-second-tour-de-l-election-presidentielle.148975.html|archive-date= 8 May 2017}}</ref>

=== Debate ===
Though TF1 initially had plans to hold its own debate between the first and second round, it instead jointly hosted one with France 2.<ref name="challenges-debat">{{cite news|author=Marc Baudriller|title=TF1 renonce à organiser son propre débat d'entre les deux tours|url=https://www.challenges.fr/election-presidentielle-2017/la-campagne-dans-les-medias/tf1-renonce-a-organiser-son-propre-debat-d-entre-les-deux-tours_464955|newspaper=Challenges|date=5 April 2017|access-date=6 April 2017|archive-date=19 October 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191019125218/https://www.challenges.fr/election-presidentielle-2017/la-campagne-dans-les-medias/tf1-renonce-a-organiser-son-propre-debat-d-entre-les-deux-tours_464955|url-status=dead}}</ref> BFM TV also originally intended to host a debate between the two rounds, and it sought to join France 2 and TF1 in co-hosting a single debate but was rebuffed; while all channels were welcome to broadcast the debate, CEO of France Télévisions [[Delphine Ernotte]] said, it would not accept such an arrangement with BFM TV, which would mean three journalists moderating the debate.<ref>{{cite news|author=Louis Hausalter|title=Débat du second tour : TF1 et France 2 refusent un plan à trois avec BFMTV|url=https://www.marianne.net/medias/debat-du-second-tour-tf1-et-france-2-refusent-un-plan-trois-avec-bfmtv|newspaper=Marianne|date=12 April 2017|access-date=19 April 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170419002629/https://www.marianne.net/medias/debat-du-second-tour-tf1-et-france-2-refusent-un-plan-trois-avec-bfmtv|archive-date=19 April 2017}}</ref> Unlike [[Jacques Chirac]], who refused to debate [[Jean-Marie Le Pen]] after the latter's surprise advancement to the second round in the [[2002 French presidential election|2002 presidential election]], Macron agreed to debate Marine Le Pen on 3 May.<ref>{{cite news|title=Présidentielle : Macron accepte de participer au débat TV de l'entre-deux-tours face à Le Pen|url=http://www.europe1.fr/politique/presidentielle-macron-accepte-de-participer-au-debat-tv-de-lentre-deux-tours-face-a-le-pen-3310136|agency=Agence France-Presse|publisher=Europe 1|date=24 April 2017|access-date=27 April 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170426055932/http://www.europe1.fr/politique/presidentielle-macron-accepte-de-participer-au-debat-tv-de-lentre-deux-tours-face-a-le-pen-3310136|archive-date=26 April 2017}}</ref> The debate, planned to start at 21:00 CEST and last 2 hours and 20 minutes, was originally to be moderated by [[Gilles Bouleau]] and [[David Pujadas]]; however, after the [[Conseil supérieur de l'audiovisuel]] (CSA) raised concerns that the moderators would both be men for the first time since 1995, the final pair of [[Christophe Jakubyszyn]] of TF1 and [[Nathalie Saint-Cricq]] of France 2 was chosen.<ref name="debatedetails">{{cite news|author=Léa Stassinet|title=Présidentielle 2017 : comment va se dérouler le débat de l'entre-deux tours ?|url=http://www.rtl.fr/actu/politique/presidentielle-2017-comment-va-se-derouler-le-debat-de-l-entre-deux-tours-7788296316|publisher=RTL|date=26 April 2017|access-date=27 April 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170427004120/http://www.rtl.fr/actu/politique/presidentielle-2017-comment-va-se-derouler-le-debat-de-l-entre-deux-tours-7788296316|archive-date=27 April 2017}}</ref> A total of 16.5 million people (60% of the audience share) watched the debate.<ref>{{cite news|title=16,5 millions de Français devant le dernier débat|url=http://www.lefigaro.fr/medias/2017/05/04/20004-20170504ARTFIG00106-165-millions-de-francais-devant-le-dernier-debat.php|newspaper=Le Figaro|date=4 May 2017|access-date=9 May 2017|url-status = live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170509104958/http://www.lefigaro.fr/medias/2017/05/04/20004-20170504ARTFIG00106-165-millions-de-francais-devant-le-dernier-debat.php|archive-date= 9 May 2017}}</ref>

The debate was considered to have significantly damaged the image of Le Pen and the FN before the second round of the election, with Le Pen criticized for being overly aggressive, arrogant, and amateur in the topics at hand, and was also attributed as a cause of the poor performance of the FN in the subsequent legislative elections.<ref>{{cite news|author=Dominique Albertini|title=Un débat et de gros dégâts pour le FN|url=http://www.liberation.fr/france/2017/08/09/un-debat-et-de-gros-degats-pour-le-fn_1589086|newspaper=Libération|date=9 August 2017|access-date=21 November 2017|archive-date=14 August 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170814215239/http://www.liberation.fr/france/2017/08/09/un-debat-et-de-gros-degats-pour-le-fn_1589086|url-status=live}}</ref>

